    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "A discussion of the nature and role of identity in our everyday lives. This was a three part podcast. The first part, presented by Brad Haas, discusses the role of humor in the collective identity of Stanford. What makes us laugh, and why do we seem to laugh at ourselves so much? The second part, presented by Zara Saraon, describes how sorority rush and the process of snap judgements perhaps gives us more insight into individual identity than previously thought. The third part, presented by Minna Xiao, describes the importance of the identity of space, particularly with regard to how it affects art and cultural expression. This was the final project of PWR2CG Spring 2014, The Sounds of Stanford.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Haas, Bradley and Xiao, Minna and Saraon, Zara. (2014). Sounds of Stanford Episode 12 - Identity. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/gd674nd7389",
